diff --git a/repo/generators/1d2e86233750/notes.md b/repo/generators/1d2e86233750/notes.md
--- a/repo/generators/1d2e86233750/notes.md
+++ b/repo/generators/1d2e86233750/notes.md
@@ -2,3 +2,18 @@
 
 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Learnability repair — `review-778e2a1a9f50a04c`
+
+### Finding
+
+The version-1.2.0 sampler chose A→B transforms independently at random. Across 96 consecutive three-demo/one-query lesson windows, seven windows allowed a fixed-transform rival to fit every visible demonstration and disagree on the query. Merely cycling the latent transform code was insufficient because symmetric C shapes could make a wrong transform produce the same query output.
+
+### Repair
+
+Version 1.3.0 schedules transform codes by `sample_index mod 4` and rejects C shapes unless their four supported transformed outputs are pairwise distinct. Thus every consecutive three-demo window exposes three distinct transforms, and every wrong fixed transform changes C whenever its code is wrong.
+
+### Evidence and limit
+
+The retained before/after probe checked 96 lesson windows and 77 protected-Racket labels per source. Ambiguous windows fell from 7 to 0; final transform exposure is exactly 96 occurrences for each code. The probe covers only four fixed-transform rivals and consecutive three-demo windows. Owner selection/integration of this optional peer repair remains pending.
+
