+## Learnability repair — `review-778e2a1a9f50a04c`
+
+### Finding
+
+The version-1.2.1 sampler generated down-right red pairs but no horizontal, vertical, or anti-diagonal two-cell decoys. Consequently the wrong rule “recolor every isolated 8-connected red component of size two” matched all four canonical labels, all 120 sampled labels, and all 120 tested three-demo windows, while disagreeing on a lawful orientation-decoy query.
+
+### Repair
+
+Version 1.3.0 constructively includes one exact two-cell non-target decoy in every ordinary draw, cycling horizontal, vertical, and anti-diagonal orientations by sample index. Targets remain exact down-right runs, so the canonical orientation rule is unchanged.
+
+### Evidence and limit
+
+The retained before/after probe checked 120 draws, 120 adversarial-query lesson windows, and 77 protected-Racket labels per source. Shortcut matches and ambiguous windows both fell from 120 to 0; final decoy counts were 42 horizontal, 39 vertical, and 39 anti-diagonal. The probe covers one named component-size rival and one lawful adversarial query. Owner selection/integration of this optional peer repair remains pending.
+
